---@field gcpSecretManagerSecretUri? string The URI configures a secret from [Secret Manager](https://cloud.google.com/secret-manager) in the format "projects/$PROJECT_ID/secrets/$SECRET_NAME/versions/$VERSION" for global secret or "projects/$PROJECT_ID/locations/$REGION/secrets/$SECRET_NAME/versions/$VERSION" for regional secret. Version can be fixed (e.g. "2") or "latest"

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfigList gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfig[]

---CertificateConfigPair configures pairs of certificates, which is used for client certificate and key pairs under a registry.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfigPair
---@field key? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfig Key configures the client private key. Optional.
---@field cert? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfig Cert configures the client certificate.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfigPairList gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CertificateConfigPair[]

---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CheckAutopilotCompatibilityProjectsLocationsClustersRequest
---@field name string The name (project, location, cluster) of the cluster to retrieve. Specified in the format `projects/*/locations/*/clusters/*`.

---CheckAutopilotCompatibilityResponse has a list of compatibility issues.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CheckAutopilotCompatibilityResponse
---@field issues? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AutopilotCompatibilityIssueList The list of issues for the given operation.
---@field summary? string The summary of the autopilot compatibility response.

---CidrBlock contains an optional name and one CIDR block.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CidrBlock
---@field cidrBlock? string cidr_block must be specified in CIDR notation.
---@field displayName? string display_name is an optional field for users to identify CIDR blocks.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CidrBlockList gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CidrBlock[]

---Configuration for client certificates on the cluster.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClientCertificateConfig
---@field issueClientCertificate? boolean Issue a client certificate.

---Configuration options for the Cloud Run feature.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CloudRunConfig
---@field loadBalancerType? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CloudRunConfigLoadBalancerTypeEnum|string Which load balancer type is installed for Cloud Run.
---@field disabled? boolean Whether Cloud Run addon is enabled for this cluster.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CloudRunConfigLoadBalancerTypeEnum "LOAD_BALANCER_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOAD_BALANCER_TYPE_EXTERNAL"|"LOAD_BALANCER_TYPE_INTERNAL"

---A Google Kubernetes Engine cluster.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Cluster
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. Deprecated. Use conditions instead. Additional information about the current status of this cluster, if available.
---@field podSecurityPolicyConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.PodSecurityPolicyConfig Configuration for the PodSecurityPolicy feature.
---@field resourceUsageExportConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ResourceUsageExportConfig Configuration for exporting resource usages. Resource usage export is disabled when this config unspecified.
---@field userManagedKeysConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.UserManagedKeysConfig The Custom keys configuration for the cluster.
---@field podAutoscaling? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.PodAutoscaling The config for pod autoscaling.
---@field nodeConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodeConfig Parameters used in creating the cluster's nodes. For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a "node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the "initial_node_count") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time. For responses, this field will be populated with the node configuration of the first node pool. (For configuration of each node pool, see `node_pool.config`) If unspecified, the defaults are used. This field is deprecated, use node_pool.config instead.
---@field currentEmulatedVersion? string Output only. The current emulated version of the master endpoint. The version is in minor version format, e.g. 1.30. No value or empty string means the cluster has no emulated version.
---@field network? string The name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to which the cluster is connected. If left unspecified, the `default` network will be used. On output this shows the network ID instead of the name.
---@field binaryAuthorization? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.BinaryAuthorization Configuration for Binary Authorization.
---@field monitoringService? string The monitoring service the cluster should use to write metrics. Currently available options: * `monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Monitoring service with a Kubernetes-native resource model * `monitoring.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Monitoring service (no longer available as of GKE 1.15). * `none` - No metrics will be exported from the cluster. If left as an empty string,`monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be used for GKE 1.14+ or `monitoring.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.
---@field scheduleUpgradeConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ScheduleUpgradeConfig Optional. Configuration for scheduled upgrades.
---@field nodePools? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolList The node pools associated with this cluster. This field should not be set if "node_config" or "initial_node_count" are specified.
---@field initialNodeCount? number The number of nodes to create in this cluster. You must ensure that your Compute Engine [resource quota](https://cloud.google.com/compute/quotas) is sufficient for this number of instances. You must also have available firewall and routes quota. For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a "node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the "node_config") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time. This field is deprecated, use node_pool.initial_node_count instead.
---@field confidentialNodes? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ConfidentialNodes Configuration of Confidential Nodes. All the nodes in the cluster will be Confidential VM once enabled.
---@field nodePoolDefaults? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolDefaults Default NodePool settings for the entire cluster. These settings are overridden if specified on the specific NodePool object.
---@field managedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig Configuration for managed machine learning diagnostics.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field defaultMaxPodsConstraint? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MaxPodsConstraint The default constraint on the maximum number of pods that can be run simultaneously on a node in the node pool of this cluster. Only honored if cluster created with IP Alias support.
---@field currentNodeCount? number Output only. The number of nodes currently in the cluster. Deprecated. Call Kubernetes API directly to retrieve node information.
---@field name? string The name of this cluster. The name must be unique within this project and location (e.g. zone or region), and can be up to 40 characters with the following restrictions: * Lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens only. * Must start with a letter. * Must end with a number or a letter.
---@field initialClusterVersion? string The initial Kubernetes version for this cluster. Valid versions are those found in validMasterVersions returned by getServerConfig. The version can be upgraded over time; such upgrades are reflected in currentMasterVersion and currentNodeVersion. Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior: - "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version - "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version - "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version - "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version - "","-": picks the default Kubernetes version
---@field enableTpu? boolean Enable the ability to use Cloud TPUs in this cluster. This field is deprecated, use tpu_config.enabled instead. This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.
---@field authenticatorGroupsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AuthenticatorGroupsConfig Configuration controlling RBAC group membership information.
---@field alphaClusterFeatureGates? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringList The list of user specified Kubernetes feature gates. Each string represents the activation status of a feature gate (e.g. "featureX=true" or "featureX=false")
---@field masterAuthorizedNetworksConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig The configuration options for master authorized networks feature. Deprecated: Use ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig.IPEndpointsConfig.authorized_networks_config instead.
---@field securityPostureConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.SecurityPostureConfig Optional. Enable/Disable Security Posture API features for the cluster.
---@field compliancePostureConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CompliancePostureConfig Optional. Deprecated: Compliance Posture is no longer supported. For more details, see https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/deprecations/posture-management-deprecation. Enable/Disable Compliance Posture features for the cluster.
---@field targetNodeVersion? string Optional. The cluster-level default node version to be used for newly created node pools where the node version is not explicitly specified. The node version is also used to reconcile existing node pools to this version.
---@field nodeIpv4CidrSize? number Output only. The size of the address space on each node for hosting containers. This is provisioned from within the `container_ipv4_cidr` range. This field will only be set when cluster is in route-based network mode.
---@field zone? string Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine [zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster resides. This field is deprecated, use location instead.
---@field releaseChannel? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ReleaseChannel Release channel configuration. If left unspecified on cluster creation and a version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the most mature release channel where the version is available (first checking STABLE, then REGULAR, and finally RAPID). Otherwise, if no release channel configuration and no version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the REGULAR channel with its default version.
---@field subnetwork? string The name of the Google Compute Engine [subnetwork](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/subnetworks) to which the cluster is connected. On output this shows the subnetwork ID instead of the name.
---@field clusterIpv4Cidr? string The IP address range of the container pods in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `10.96.0.0/14`). Leave blank to have one automatically chosen or specify a `/14` block in `10.0.0.0/8`.
---@field monitoringConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MonitoringConfig Monitoring configuration for the cluster.
---@field resourceLabels? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringMap The resource labels for the cluster to use to annotate any related Google Compute Engine resources.
---@field locations? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringList The list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster's nodes should be located. This field provides a default value if [NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations) are not specified during node pool creation. Warning: changing cluster locations will update the [NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations) of all node pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.
---@field secretManagerConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.SecretManagerConfig Secret CSI driver configuration.
---@field location? string Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine [zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available) or [region](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available) in which the cluster resides.
---@field loggingService? string The logging service the cluster should use to write logs. Currently available options: * `logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Logging service with a Kubernetes-native resource model * `logging.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Logging service (no longer available as of GKE 1.15). * `none` - no logs will be exported from the cluster. If left as an empty string,`logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be used for GKE 1.14+ or `logging.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.
---@field workloadIdentityConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.WorkloadIdentityConfig Configuration for the use of Kubernetes Service Accounts in IAM policies.
---@field master? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Master Configuration for master components.
---@field enableK8sBetaApis? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Kubernetes open source beta apis enabled on the cluster. Only beta apis.
---@field gkeAutoUpgradeConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.GkeAutoUpgradeConfig Configuration for GKE auto upgrades.
---@field currentMasterVersion? string Output only. The current software version of the master endpoint.
---@field controlPlaneEndpointsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig Configuration for all cluster's control plane endpoints.
---@field autoscaling? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscaling Cluster-level autoscaling configuration.
---@field etag? string This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of cluster fields, and may be sent on update requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding.
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MaintenancePolicy Configure the maintenance policy for this cluster.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterStatusEnum|string Output only. The current status of this cluster.
---@field verticalPodAutoscaling? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.VerticalPodAutoscaling Cluster-level Vertical Pod Autoscaling configuration.
---@field networkConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NetworkConfig Configuration for cluster networking.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the cluster was created, in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field secretSyncConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.SecretSyncConfig Configuration for sync Secret Manager secrets as k8s secrets.
---@field workloadAltsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.WorkloadALTSConfig Configuration for direct-path (via ALTS) with workload identity. This feature is not officially supported for external customers in Kubernetes Engine when using Workload Identity.
---@field workloadCertificates? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.WorkloadCertificates Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes pods.
---@field tpuConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.TpuConfig Configuration for Cloud TPU support; This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.
---@field nodePoolUpgradeConcurrencyConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolUpgradeConcurrencyConfig The node pool upgrade concurrency config of the cluster. This field is used for auto upgrade.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field id? string Output only. Unique id for the cluster.
---@field nodePoolAutoConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolAutoConfig Node pool configs that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters.
---@field protectConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ProtectConfig Deprecated: Use SecurityPostureConfig instead. Enable/Disable Protect API features for the cluster.
---@field nodeCreationConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodeCreationConfig Optional. Configuration for Node Creation Mode.
---@field shieldedNodes? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ShieldedNodes Shielded Nodes configuration.
---@field notificationConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NotificationConfig Notification configuration of the cluster.
---@field controlPlaneEgress? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ControlPlaneEgress Configuration for control plane egress control.
---@field servicesIpv4Cidr? string Output only. The IP address range of the Kubernetes services in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `1.2.3.4/29`). Service addresses are typically put in the last `/16` from the container CIDR.
---@field anonymousAuthenticationConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AnonymousAuthenticationConfig Configuration for limiting anonymous access to all endpoints except the health checks.
---@field databaseEncryption? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.DatabaseEncryption Configuration of etcd encryption.
---@field endpoint? string Output only. The IP address of this cluster's master endpoint. The endpoint can be accessed from the internet at `https://username:password@endpoint/`. See the `masterAuth` property of this resource for username and password information.
---@field privateClusterConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.PrivateClusterConfig Configuration for private cluster.
---@field ipAllocationPolicy? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.IPAllocationPolicy Configuration for cluster IP allocation.
---@field currentNodeVersion? string Output only. Deprecated, use [NodePool.version](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1beta1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools) instead. The current version of the node software components. If they are currently at multiple versions because they're in the process of being upgraded, this reflects the minimum version of all nodes.
---@field rollbackSafeUpgrade? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.RollbackSafeUpgrade The rollback safe upgrade information of the cluster. This field is used when user manually triggers a rollback safe upgrade.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StatusConditionList Which conditions caused the current cluster state.
---@field masterAuth? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MasterAuth The authentication information for accessing the master endpoint. If unspecified, the defaults are used: For clusters before v1.12, if master_auth is unspecified, `username` will be set to "admin", a random password will be generated, and a client certificate will be issued.
---@field description? string An optional description of this cluster.
---@field privateCluster? boolean If this is a private cluster setup. Private clusters are clusters that, by default have no external IP addresses on the nodes and where nodes and the master communicate over private IP addresses. This field is deprecated, use private_cluster_config.enable_private_nodes instead.
---@field tpuIpv4CidrBlock? string Output only. The IP address range of the Cloud TPUs in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `1.2.3.4/29`). This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.
---@field loggingConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.LoggingConfig Logging configuration for the cluster.
---@field enterpriseConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.EnterpriseConfig GKE Enterprise Configuration. Deprecated: GKE Enterprise features are now available without an Enterprise tier.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labelFingerprint? string The fingerprint of the set of labels for this cluster.
---@field masterIpv4CidrBlock? string The IP prefix in CIDR notation to use for the hosted master network. This prefix will be used for assigning private IP addresses to the master or set of masters, as well as the ILB VIP. This field is deprecated, use private_cluster_config.master_ipv4_cidr_block instead.
---@field parentProductConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ParentProductConfig The configuration of the parent product of the cluster. This field is used by Google internal products that are built on top of the GKE cluster and take the ownership of the cluster.
---@field addonsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AddonsConfig Configurations for the various addons available to run in the cluster.
---@field meshCertificates? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.MeshCertificates Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes pods.
---@field rbacBindingConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.RBACBindingConfig RBACBindingConfig allows user to restrict ClusterRoleBindings an RoleBindings that can be created.
---@field enableKubernetesAlpha? boolean Kubernetes alpha features are enabled on this cluster. This includes alpha API groups (e.g. v1beta1) and features that may not be production ready in the kubernetes version of the master and nodes. The cluster has no SLA for uptime and master/node upgrades are disabled. Alpha enabled clusters are automatically deleted thirty days after creation.
---@field instanceGroupUrls? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringList Output only. Deprecated. Use node_pools.instance_group_urls.
---@field managedOpentelemetryConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ManagedOpenTelemetryConfig Configuration for Managed OpenTelemetry pipeline.
---@field fleet? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Fleet Fleet information for the cluster.
---@field identityServiceConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.IdentityServiceConfig Configuration for Identity Service component.
---@field costManagementConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.CostManagementConfig Configuration for the fine-grained cost allocation feature.
---@field legacyAbac? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.LegacyAbac Configuration for the legacy ABAC authorization mode.
---@field clusterTelemetry? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterTelemetry Telemetry integration for the cluster.
---@field autopilot? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Autopilot Autopilot configuration for the cluster.
---@field networkPolicy? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NetworkPolicy Configuration options for the NetworkPolicy feature.
---@field expireTime? string Output only. The time the cluster will be automatically deleted in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.

---ClusterAutoscaling contains global, per-cluster information required by Cluster Autoscaler to automatically adjust the size of the cluster and create/delete node pools based on the current needs.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscaling
---@field enableNodeAutoprovisioning? boolean Enables automatic node pool creation and deletion.
---@field autopilotGeneralProfile? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscalingAutopilotGeneralProfileEnum|string Autopilot general profile for the cluster, which defines the configuration for the cluster.
---@field autoscalingProfile? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscalingAutoscalingProfileEnum|string Defines autoscaling behaviour.
---@field defaultComputeClassConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.DefaultComputeClassConfig Default compute class is a configuration for default compute class.
---@field autoprovisioningLocations? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringList The list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the NodePool's nodes can be created by NAP.
---@field autoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults contains defaults for a node pool created by NAP.
---@field resourceLimits? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ResourceLimitList Contains global constraints regarding minimum and maximum amount of resources in the cluster.
---@field autoprovisioningRestrictionConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AutoprovisioningRestrictionConfig Optional. Configures restrictions related to autoprovisioning settings.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscalingAutopilotGeneralProfileEnum "AUTOPILOT_GENERAL_PROFILE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_PERFORMANCE"|"NONE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterAutoscalingAutoscalingProfileEnum "PROFILE_UNSPECIFIED"|"OPTIMIZE_UTILIZATION"|"BALANCED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterList gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Cluster[]

---Configuration of all network bandwidth tiers
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfig
---@field totalEgressBandwidthTier? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfigTotalEgressBandwidthTierEnum|string Specifies the total network bandwidth tier for the NodePool.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfigTotalEgressBandwidthTierEnum "TIER_UNSPECIFIED"|"TIER_1"

---ClusterPolicyConfig stores the configuration for cluster wide policies.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterPolicyConfig
---@field noSystemMutation? boolean Denotes that preventing creation and mutation of resources in GKE managed namespaces and cluster-scoped GKE managed resources .
---@field noUnsafeWebhooks? boolean Denotes preventing unsafe webhooks.
---@field noStandardNodePools? boolean Denotes preventing standard node pools and requiring only autopilot node pools.
---@field noSystemImpersonation? boolean Denotes preventing impersonation and CSRs for GKE System users.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROVISIONING"|"RUNNING"|"RECONCILING"|"STOPPING"|"ERROR"|"DEGRADED"

---Telemetry integration for the cluster.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterTelemetry
---@field type? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterTelemetryTypeEnum|string Type of the integration.

---@alias gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterTelemetryTypeEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"DISABLED"|"ENABLED"|"SYSTEM_ONLY"

---ClusterUpdate describes an update to the cluster. Exactly one update can be applied to a cluster with each request, so at most one field can be provided.
---@class gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterUpdate
---@field desiredGcfsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.GcfsConfig The desired GCFS config for the cluster.
---@field desiredImageType? string The desired image type for the node pool. NOTE: Set the "desired_node_pool" field as well.
---@field desiredDisableL4LbFirewallReconciliation? boolean Enable/Disable L4 LB VPC firewall reconciliation for the cluster.
---@field desiredMaster? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.Master Configuration for master components.
---@field desiredNodeCreationConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodeCreationConfig Optional. The desired NodeCreationConfig for the cluster.
---@field desiredMasterVersion? string The Kubernetes version to change the master to. The only valid value is the latest supported version. Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior: - "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version - "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version - "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version - "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version - "-": picks the default Kubernetes version
---@field desiredUserManagedKeysConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.UserManagedKeysConfig The desired user managed keys config for the cluster.
---@field desiredK8sBetaApis? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Beta APIs enabled for cluster.
---@field desiredWorkloadIdentityConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.WorkloadIdentityConfig Configuration for Workload Identity.
---@field desiredEnablePrivateEndpoint? boolean Enable/Disable private endpoint for the cluster's master. Deprecated: Use desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.enable_public_endpoint instead. Note that the value of enable_public_endpoint is reversed: if enable_private_endpoint is false, then enable_public_endpoint will be true.
---@field privateClusterConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.PrivateClusterConfig The desired private cluster configuration. Has no effect. Use desired_private_cluster_config instead.
---@field desiredEmulatedVersion? string Optional. The desired emulated version for the cluster.
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoscaling? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolAutoscaling Autoscaler configuration for the node pool specified in desired_node_pool_id. If there is only one pool in the cluster and desired_node_pool_id is not provided then the change applies to that single node pool.
---@field desiredAutoIpamConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.AutoIpamConfig AutoIpamConfig contains all information related to Auto IPAM
---@field desiredImageProject? string The project containing the desired image to use for this node. This is used to create clusters using a custom image.
---@field desiredNodePoolLoggingConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.NodePoolLoggingConfig The desired node pool logging configuration defaults for the cluster.
---@field desiredAdditionalIpRangesConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.DesiredAdditionalIPRangesConfig The desired config for additional subnetworks attached to the cluster.
---@field desiredContainerdConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ContainerdConfig The desired containerd config for the cluster.
---@field desiredInTransitEncryptionConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ClusterUpdateDesiredInTransitEncryptionConfigEnum|string Specify the details of in-transit encryption. Now named inter-node transparent encryption.
---@field desiredManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig The desired managed machine learning diagnostics configuration.
---@field desiredScheduleUpgradeConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ScheduleUpgradeConfig Optional. The desired scheduled upgrades configuration for the cluster.
---@field desiredDnsConfig? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.DNSConfig DNSConfig contains clusterDNS config for this cluster.
---@field desiredLocations? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.StringList The desired list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster's nodes should be located. This list must always include the cluster's primary zone. Warning: changing cluster locations will update the locations of all node pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoConfigResourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.ResourceManagerTags The desired resource manager tags that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters.
---@field enableK8sBetaApis? gcp.unstable.container_v1beta1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Kubernetes open source beta apis enabled on the cluster. Only beta apis
